         <div type="bio">
            <p>American publisher. A native Canadian, Marshall had a brief publishing career in New York, first in partnership with Laurence J. Gomme in 1915, and then on his own. In 1916 he published Alfred Kreymborg’s <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Mushrooms: A Book of Free Forms</name>, and two issues of <name type="work" key="ID_MISSING">Others: A Magazine of the Free Verse</name>. In March 1916 Ezra Pound interested Marshall in publishing <name type="work" key="W_APORTRAIT">A Portrait of the Artist as a Young Man</name>. Marshall sent JJ an advance of £10, but in July suddenly left New York for Quebec. <hi rend="bold">William Brockman</hi>
                </p>
         </div>
